From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Satoshi Ikeuchi <satosan.ikm@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: ath11k: describe IPQ9574 interrupt layout

Add the IPQ9574 compatible proposed for ath11k support. Describe its
interrupt layout separately from IPQ8074 and IPQ6018: the observed
IPQ9574-family interface omits the watchdog interrupt and provides a
fourth transmit-completion ring. Both layouts contain 52 interrupts.

Keep the existing SoC schemas unchanged and require named interrupts
for the IPQ9574 interface.

Link: https://lists.infradead.org/pipermail/ath11k/2026-January/008112.html
Signed-off-by: Satoshi Ikeuchi <satosan.ikm@gmail.com>
---
 .../bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath11k.yaml | 119 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 119 insertions(+)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath11k.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath11k.yaml
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
       - qcom,ipq8074-wifi
+      - qcom,ipq9574-wifi
       - qcom,ipq6018-wifi
       - qcom,wcn6750-wifi
       - qcom,ipq5018-wifi
@@ -217,6 +218,124 @@ allOf:
 
   - if:
       properties:
+        compatible:
+          contains:
+            const: qcom,ipq9574-wifi
+    then:
+      properties:
+        interrupts:
+          items:
+            - description: misc-pulse1 interrupt events
+            - description: misc-latch interrupt events
+            - description: sw exception interrupt events
+            - description: interrupt event for ring CE0
+            - description: interrupt event for ring CE1
